/-!
# Stacks 0FH5: zero cycles are generated by closed points with separable residue field

Let `k` be a field and `X` a smooth projective scheme over `k`. [Stacks, Tag 0FH5] says that
`CH_0(X)` is generated by the classes of the closed points of `X` with residue field separable
over `k`. `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.ZeroCyclesSeparablePoints` reduces this to a
statement about one closed point `x`: there are zero cycles `Z`, `Z'` supported on separable
closed points with `[x] + [Z] = [Z']`;
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.ZeroCyclesSeparableReduction` reduces that in turn to an
integral `X` carrying an ample invertible `ℒ`. This file proves the remaining statement,
following Steps 3 to 8 of the source.

If `κ(x)/k` is separable there is nothing to do. Otherwise `k` is not perfect, hence infinite.
Let `d = dim X`. For `n ≫ 0`, by [Stacks, Tag 0FD5] the sections `V ⊂ Γ(X, ℒ^{⊗ n})` vanishing at
`x` generate `ℒ^{⊗ n}` off `x` and embed `X ∖ x` in `𝐏(V)`, all sections embed `X`, and the germs
of `V` span `𝔪_x ℒ^{⊗ n}_x`. Iterating [Stacks, Tag 0FD6] (with rational members, which exist as
`k` is infinite) gives `s_1, …, s_d ∈ V` whose images in `𝔪_x/𝔪_x^2` are independent, such that
every `H_1 ∩ ⋯ ∩ H_j` is smooth off `x` of dimension `d - j` there; so the stalk at `x` of
`H_1 ∩ ⋯ ∩ H_d` is the residue field and `H_1 ∩ ⋯ ∩ H_d = x ⊔ Z` with `Z` étale over `k`. The
same with all sections gives `Z' = H'_1 ∩ ⋯ ∩ H'_d` étale over `k`. Both chains are proper
divisor cuts by sections of one invertible sheaf, so by [Stacks, Tag 02SQ] their classes agree:
`[x] + [Z] = [Z']`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.integralComplementaryCycles`: Steps 3 to 8 of the source.
* `Stacks.Chow.mem_closure_separablePointClasses_of_isProjectiveMorphism`: **Stacks 0FH5**.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FH5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FH5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FD5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FD5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FD6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FD6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02SQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02SQ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite Stacks.Ample
